<section id="measure">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">How results get reported</p>
        <h2>We won't promise you a number. We'll establish one, then move it.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="sub">Anyone who tells you what they'll make you before they've seen your store is guessing. Here's the shape of the conversation instead.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="measure">
      <div>
        <div class="chain"><span>Baseline</span><span>KPI</span><span>Implementation</span><span>Adoption</span><span>Result</span></div>
        <p>Before we build anything, we record where the number stands today. We agree on which number the implementation is supposed to move, and by when. Then we ship it, watch whether your people actually use it, and report what happened.</p>
        <p>If the number doesn't move, that's the report. We'd rather tell you a workflow underperformed and fix it than manage the reporting.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <table class="ftable">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Internet leads, one month</th><th scope="col">Baseline</th><th scope="col">After</th></tr></thead>
